% DRAFT bounded mathematical contract for YM-T15.
% Not yet registered in a crate architecture; no code generated from this file.
% The implementing agent resolves the owning qft-symbolics unit and maps it.

Implement a reusable bounded symbolic group-word/trace capability using caller
supplied typed generators, inverse orientations, group/representation assumptions,
positive matrix dimension and an explicit complex-trace vs normalized-real-trace kind.
Reuse existing exact scalar, ordered-algebra and resource-budget infrastructure.

<contract_rules>
R1(MUST): Preserve factor order; reduce only justified adjacent inverse pairs.
The inverse of a product reverses order and inverts each factor.
R2(MUST): Support trace cyclicity and justified cyclic reductions. MUST NOT
sort generic generators or equate arbitrary permutations. Equality is under
declared rules; differing forms alone do not prove matrix-trace inequality.
R3(MUST): Keep complex trace and normalized real trace distinct. Tr(I)=m;
normalized ReTr(I)=1. For declared unitary words, Tr(W^-1)=conjugate(Tr(W));
only real trace identifies those without conjugation. Real trace is real-linear,
not complex-linear. First bounded scalar domain may be exact real rationals.
R4(MUST): Retain unitarity/group/representation assumptions and explicit errors
for invalid dimensions/domains or exhausted budgets. No silent numeric fallback.
R5(MUST NOT): Hardcode a textbook equation, source filename, known expected
answer or lattice size in production algebra. Geometry is a consumer.
R6(MUST): A caller-supplied four-link gauge-transformation fixture reduces to
basepoint conjugation; trace invariance applies to a closed path. No automatic
open-path gauge-invariance assertion.
R7(MUST NOT): Implement Haar integration, Monte Carlo, CUDA or proof claims in
this unit. Source locators are provenance, not algorithmic input.
</contract_rules>

Independent fixtures:3-Pauli traces2 vs-2; SU3 diag(i,i,-1) complex trace and
inverse; two-factor cyclicity; normalized/raw identity traces; fresh names;
changed assumptions; invalid dimensions; resource limits; input nonmutation.
Use explicit matrix arithmetic independent of the production rewrite engine.
